Subject: Light-frame calls

What this does
  Light-frame calls.

Why we need it
  Every JS-to-JS call built a full heap-style record: a `JSRegRun`, an embedded `JSStackFrame`, a `memcpy` undefined fill.

What it adds
  A light frame is only the 9-slot `JSRegRun` prefix plus the variable area and register file, laid in the frame arena; no `JSStackFrame` and no record tail. `JSRegRun` is reordered so the prefix is first and `ret_dst`/`argc`/`flags`/`nctl` pack into one word; `cap_ip` carries the frame's pc and a `JSStackFrame.rv_rec` back-pointer lets `regvm_frame_pc` reach an activation's C-stack entry record (which `regvm_rec_of_sf` cannot map back from an arena frame); `rt->regvm_cur` plus `JSStackFrame.rv_light` publish the light chain and every real-frame push/pop saves and restores it, including all three `js_regvm_execute` exit paths (`done`, `done_generator` and the nested unwind) that bypass `JS_CallInternal`'s pop; the DRC root walk, `build_backtrace`, `is_strict_mode` and `JS_GetActiveFunction` walk the logical stack. New frameless `regvm_t_call_light`/`_call_method_light`; the trivial light return is fused into `regvm_t_return` and `regvm_t_return_undefined` so the value moves straight into the caller's register instead of round-tripping through the frame's `ret` slot, and `regvm_t_return_light_nested`/`regvm_t_return_light_chunk` and the unwinder arm release the variable area.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
